IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4, ss 61ZA, 61ZB, 61ZC (part ssc3).
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- These three sections sit late in the Act's order (after s 61) but section 43 needs them, so this
-- module comes first and ssc3-a-s43-s44.l4 imports it.
--
-- A "unit of additional pension" is a fact about the person (the count is an input; s 14A, in
-- ssc1's range, says how units arise). "The relevant contribution conditions" are the conditions for
-- the pension asked about; whether the person would be entitled if they were satisfied is a
-- counterfactual that the person states.

§ `Part II: shortfall in contributions, people with units of additional pension`

§§ `Section 61ZA: shortfall in contributions, people with units of additional pension`

-- "applies to a person ... if" the person has units, is not entitled to a Category A retirement
-- pension, but would be if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied.
-- src:1839 | (1) This section applies to a person who has one or more units of additional pension if the person—
-- src:1840 | (a) is not entitled to a Category A retirement pension, but
-- src:1841 | (b) would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied.
@ref s 61ZA(1) (src:1839-1841)
GIVEN `the number of units of additional pension the person has` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a person who has one or more units of additional pension if the person" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a), NOTES.md)
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (`the number of units of additional pension the person has` AT LEAST 1)
          , JUST (NOT `the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension`)
          , `the person would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied`)

-- The relevant contribution conditions "are to be taken to be satisfied". The text says it only for
-- the person to whom the section applies; for anyone else it is silent.
-- src:1842 | (2) The relevant contribution conditions are to be taken to be satisfied for the purposes of the person's entitlement to a Category A retirement pension.
@ref s 61ZA(2) (src:1842)
GIVEN `s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61ZA(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for "the purposes of the person's entitlement" in the s 61ZA(1) case only
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): s 61ZA(1)(b) is a counterfactual the person has not answered

-- "the only element of that pension to which the person is so entitled is the additional pension
-- attributable to the units of additional pension".
-- src:1843 | (3) But where a person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension because of this section, the only element of that pension to which the person is so entitled is the additional pension attributable to the units of additional pension.
@ref s 61ZA(3) (src:1843)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension because of section 61ZA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the additional pension attributable to the units in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 61ZA(3) the weekly rate of the pension the person is entitled to because of section 61ZA` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension because of section 61ZA`
    THEN JUST `the weekly rate of the additional pension attributable to the units in pounds`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of "a person [who] is entitled to a Category A retirement pension because of this section"

§§ `Section 61ZB: shortfall in contributions, people whose dead spouse had units of additional pension`

-- "applies to a person whose spouse or civil partner died with one or more units of additional
-- pension if the person" is not entitled to a Category B pension as a result of the death but would
-- be if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied.
-- src:1846 | (1) This section applies to a person whose spouse or civil partner died with one or more units of additional pension if the person—
-- src:1847 | (a) is not entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death, but
-- src:1848 | (b) would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied.
@ref s 61ZB(1) (src:1846-1848)
GIVEN `the number of units of additional pension the dead spouse or civil partner had` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61ZB(1) this section applies to the person` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a person whose spouse or civil partner died with one or more units of additional pension if the person" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (`the number of units of additional pension the dead spouse or civil partner had` AT LEAST 1)
          , JUST (NOT `the person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death`)
          , `the person would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied`)

-- src:1849 | (2) The relevant contribution conditions are to be taken to be satisfied for the purposes of the person's entitlement to that Category B retirement pension.
@ref s 61ZB(2) (src:1849)
GIVEN `s 61ZB(1) this section applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61ZB(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 61ZB(1) this section applies to the person`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for "the person's entitlement to that Category B retirement pension" in the s 61ZB(1) case only
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): s 61ZB(1)(b) is a counterfactual the person has not answered

-- src:1850 | (3) But where a person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension because of this section, the only element of that pension to which the person is so entitled is the additional pension attributable to the units of additional pension.
@ref s 61ZB(3) (src:1850)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension because of section 61ZB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the additional pension attributable to the units in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 61ZB(3) the weekly rate of the pension the person is entitled to because of section 61ZB` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension because of section 61ZB`
    THEN JUST `the weekly rate of the additional pension attributable to the units in pounds`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of "a person [who] is entitled to a Category B retirement pension because of this section"

§§ `Section 61ZC: entitlement to more than one pension, sections 61ZA and 61ZB`

-- Section 43 does not prevent both the Category A pension (because of s 61ZA) and one Category B pension.
-- Not a "no": the sentence only lifts the s 43(1) bar in this case.
-- src:1853 | (1) Section 43 does not prevent a person from being entitled for the same period to both—
-- src:1854 | (a) a Category A retirement pension because of section 61ZA, and
-- src:1855 | (b) one Category B retirement pension.
@ref s 61ZC(1) (src:1853-1855)
GIVEN `the person has a Category A retirement pension because of section 61ZA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Category B retirement pensions the person has` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61ZC(1) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` MEANS
    IF `the person has a Category A retirement pension because of section 61ZA` AND `the number of Category B retirement pensions the person has` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the lifting of the bar is for "a Category A retirement pension because of section 61ZA" together with "one Category B retirement pension"

-- Section 43 does not prevent both a Category A pension and one Category B pension because of s 61ZB
-- (or, if more than one such Category B pension, the most favourable of them).
-- src:1856 | (2) Section 43 does not prevent a person from being entitled for the same period to both—
-- src:1857 | (a) a Category A retirement pension, and
-- src:1858 | (b) one Category B retirement pension because of section 61ZB (or, if there is more than one such Category B retirement pension, the most favourable of them).
@ref s 61ZC(2) (src:1856-1858)
GIVEN `the person has a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Category B retirement pensions the person has because of section 61ZB` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61ZC(2) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` MEANS
    IF `the person has a Category A retirement pension` AND `the number of Category B retirement pensions the person has because of section 61ZB` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the lifting of the bar is for "a Category A retirement pension" together with "one Category B retirement pension because of section 61ZB"

-- (3)(a): in section 43(2)(a) the reference to "a Category A or a Category B retirement pension",
-- in a case in which (1) or (2) applies, includes "a Category A and a Category B retirement pension".
-- src:1859 | (3) Accordingly—
-- src:1860 | (a) in section 43(2)(a) the reference to “a Category A or a Category B retirement pension”, in a case in which subsection (1) or (2) of this section applies, includes “a Category A and a Category B retirement pension”,
@ref s 61ZC(3)(a) (src:1859-1860)
GIVEN `s 61ZC(1) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 61ZC(2) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61ZC(3)(a) section 43(2)(a) includes a Category A and a Category B retirement pension` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the inclusion is "in a case in which subsection (1) or (2) of this section applies"
    IF `ssc3 helper any of` (LIST `s 61ZC(1) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions`, `s 61ZC(2) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3)(b): in sections 43(3)(a) and (aa), 51A and 52 "Category A retirement pension" does not include
-- a pension to which a person is entitled because of section 61ZA.
-- src:1861 | (b) in sections 43(3)(a) and (aa), 51A and 52 “Category A retirement pension” does not include a pension to which a person is entitled because of section 61ZA, and
@ref s 61ZC(3)(b) (src:1861)
GIVEN `the pension is one to which the person is entitled because of section 61ZA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61ZC(3)(b) the pension counts as a Category A retirement pension in sections 43(3)(a) and (aa), 51A and 52` MEANS
    IF `the pension is one to which the person is entitled because of section 61ZA`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"Category A retirement pension\" does not include a pension to which a person is entitled because of section 61ZA"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the term does not include; a pension not awarded under s 61ZA is left to the ordinary meaning

-- (3)(c): in sections 43(3)(a) and 52 "Category B retirement pension" does not include a pension to
-- which a person is entitled because of section 61ZB.
-- src:1862 | (c) in sections 43(3)(a) and 52 “Category B retirement pension” does not include a pension to which a person is entitled because of section 61ZB.
@ref s 61ZC(3)(c) (src:1862)
GIVEN `the pension is one to which the person is entitled because of section 61ZB` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61ZC(3)(c) the pension counts as a Category B retirement pension in sections 43(3)(a) and 52` MEANS
    IF `the pension is one to which the person is entitled because of section 61ZB`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"Category B retirement pension\" does not include a pension to which a person is entitled because of section 61ZB"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the term does not include; a pension not awarded under s 61ZB is left to the ordinary meaning
